---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site
  title="About · Ouijit"
  description="Ouijit is built by one person, Prentice Bjerkeseth. Free, open source under AGPL, no account and no telemetry, and the plan is to keep it that way.">
  <main class="compare-content about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Ouijit is a desktop app for running coding agents in parallel, each in its own git worktree. I make it
      alone, and it's free and open source under AGPL-3.0.
    </p>
    <p>
      I started it for fun, once AI was good enough to build with, and within a week I was doing all my work in
      it. It runs agents as the CLIs they are, in real terminals, because that's where their capability shows
      up first. I'll add a chat interface eventually, on top of that rather than instead of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      There's no account, because I don't think a tool like this should ask you to log in. There's no
      telemetry, because I don't think good tools should cost you your privacy. The only thing I know about how
      many people use Ouijit is how often the builds get downloaded, and I'm fine with that.
    </p>
    <p>
      If Ouijit ever charges for something, it will be a feature that costs me something to run, like hosted
      environments or sync. The app itself stays free.
    </p>
    <p>
      Many tools like this are raising venture money, getting acquired, or shutting down. I want this one to
      still be standing, still free and still private, and to show that one person can build something
      special.
    </p>
    <p class="about-sign"><a href="https://github.com/pbjer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prentice Bjerkeseth</a></p>
  </main>
</Site>
